92684405 (1484 1793411965427 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f402") (src . "context: the excluded clause's cap has rows that can go red\n\nThe excluded clause of a context answer shows each counter at most at\nthe cap and says (capped) when any count is above it, as the users\nclause does. No fixture store reaches the cap, so that branch had no\nrow that could go red: the clause was built inside finish, out of\nreach of a test.\n\nThe constructor is now a definition of its own, excluded-clause, with\nits reservation reserved-excluded a top-level definition beside\nreserved-users, and both are exported for the fixture's rows, not as\nan interface; finish calls the constructor at its one site. The answer\nis unchanged byte for byte.\n\nRows in context-users (U12): all seven counters at the cap and counts\nbelow it are shown as they are, with no marker; a count above the cap\nis shown at it and the clause says (capped), for the first counter,\nthe last beside one at the cap, and all; no clause prints longer than\nthe reservation and the all-above one is exactly it; a zero count is\nshown as 0, not left out. rows-baseline.txt carries the fixture's new\ncounts and hash.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 556))))
